 and ensure the implementation of policies, procedures and controls so that Company's compliance with employment laws is complied. This position serves as key strategic compliance partner for human resources on employment and labour compliance requirements.<br><br>About the role<br>1. Initiate and assist the relevant departments to design policies, guidelines and procedures to&nbsp;drive employment compliance across the enterprise.<br>2. Areas of scope include all company hiring practices, wages, discrimination/harassment,&nbsp;workplace violence, accessibility and other employment obligations. Monitor the&nbsp;implementation of employment compliance programs, systems and training.<br>3. Initiates cross-functional efforts to drive organizational alignment and ensure compliance&nbsp;with employment obligations.<br>4. Defines success metrics for areas of responsibility and integrates them into core business&nbsp;metrics. Monitor, evaluate and measure operational program processes for review with&nbsp;cross-functional teams to close employment compliance gaps, and drive continuous&nbsp;improvement.<br>5. Articulates corporate positions on compliance matters to regulators and external agencies&nbsp;and directs involvement with regulators to ensure compliance with all legal requirements.<br>6. Develops external relationships and alliances strengthening on the company\u2019s reputation within compliance community and leads regulatory outreach meetings, ensuring that the company\u2019s compliance programs, policies, procedures and reports are communicated in a persuasive, accurate and understandable way and that sensitive data is protected. Monitors emerging compliance requirements, including new regulations, and develops strategies to&nbsp;respond to compliance risk.<br>7. Ensures that compliance programs, policies, procedures and reporting are consistent with&nbsp;global direction and leverage global talent and resources.<br>8. Manage the development and implementation o