way and Web Platforms pod. You'll own the end-to-end design strategy for this scope, bring operational clarity to complex, multi-quarter projects, and lead and grow a team of 4\u20135 designers.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This is a high-leverage role. The Payment Gateway is how online businesses accept payments through PhonePe \u2014 the experience you design is felt by merchants and, downstream, by every customer who pays them. The details are hard, the constraints are real, and the work directly moves the business.<br><br></p>\n<h3><strong>Key Responsibilities&nbsp; (Competencies &amp; Role Expectations)</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Co-own Product Roadmaps:</strong> Work closely with leadership to understand the overarching business vision and translate it into actionable, design-first GTM strategies for our Payment Gateway and Web Platforms.</li>\n<li><strong>Mentorship &amp; Team Structuring:</strong> Manage, mentor, and scale a pod of 4-5 designers. Pivot effectively from individual contribution to strategic delegation\u2014optimizing team structures, guiding career growth, and overseeing the quality of hires.</li>\n<li><strong>Influence &amp; Partner:</strong> Build deep trust with business unit leadership. Operate as a \"first team\" with leaders by helping them achieve their functional goals through design. Proactively resolve conflicts and align stakeholders toward common objectives.</li>\n<li><strong>Build to Learn:</strong> Direct intuitive product architecture with a strong \u201cbuild to learn\u201d mindset. Emphasize continuous prototyping, synthesize insights from usability testing, and weave them into the core product strategy.</li>\n<li><strong>Drive Measurable Outcomes:</strong> Define North Star metrics for your features and utilize data to form actionable insights. Ensure that design outputs directly influence business revenue and deliver measurable results.</li>\n<li><strong>Holistic Architecture:</strong> Direct the team to take a holistic view of the product ecosystem, employing journey maps and service blueprints to align stakeholders and improve end-to-end service delivery.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Orchestrate Complex Delivery:</strong> Own the planning, triaging, and delivery of multiple large, complex projects spanning across quarters. Balance competing priorities and tactically unblock teams to deliver work faster.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Elevate Visual Systems:</strong> Deliver best-in-class, cohesive visual experiences by unifying design systems, motion, and UX copy. Foster tight feedback loops between graphics, creative, and product design teams.</li>\n<li><strong>Technical Synergy:</strong> Translate complex technical/backend capabilities into highly scalable, delightful, and user-friendly interfaces, ensuring designs exploit technical constraints to enable speed and security.</li>\n<li><strong>High-Quality Handoffs:</strong> Leverage your deep understanding of frontend systems and code as a medium. Deploy robust processes for smooth, repeatable engineering handoffs through high-touch communication and clear documentation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><strong>What We\u2019re Looking For</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>7\u201310 </strong>years of product design experience, with real ownership of complex enterprise, B2B, or fintech platforms.</li>\n<li><strong>1\u20132 years</strong> managing and scaling direct reports \u2014 you've grown designers, not just reviewed their work.</li>\n<li><strong>Proven craft: </strong>A portfolio that shows depth: interaction design, visual rigor, and clear reasoning behind each decision.</li>\n<li><strong>Technical acumen: </strong>Deep comfort navigating technical constraints to design scalable, developer-friendly interfaces. You speak engineering's language.</li>\n<li><strong>Systems thinking: </strong>You design for the whole product and are fluent with design systems \u2014 when to extend one and when to break from it.</li>\n<li><strong>Strong communication: You</strong> write clear UX copy, make a tight case for a direction, and give direct, useful feedback. You manage stakeholders without losing the user's point of view.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Design Microsite Link :&nbsp;<a href=\"https://design.phonepe.com/\">https://design.phonepe.com/</a><br></strong></p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><strong>PhonePe Full Time Employee Benefits (Not applicable for Intern or Contract Roles)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Insurance Benefits - </strong>Medical Insurance, Critical Illness Insurance, Accidental Insurance, Life Insurance</li>\n<li><strong>Wellness Program -</strong> Employee Assistance Program, Onsite Medical Center, Emergency Support System</li>\n<li><strong>Parental Support - </strong>Maternity Benefit, Paternity Benefit Program, Adoption Assistance Program, Day-care Support Program</li>\n<li><strong>Mobility Benefits - </strong>Relocation benefits, Transfer Support Policy, Travel Policy</li>\n<li><strong>Retirement Benefits - </strong>Employee PF Contribution, Flexible PF Contribution, Gratuity, NPS, Leave Encashment&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong>Other Benefits - </strong>Higher Education Assistance, Car Lease, Salary Advance Policy</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><em>Our inclusive culture promotes individual expression, creativity, innovation, and achievement and in turn helps us better understand and serve our customers. We see ourselves as a place for intellectual curiosity,&nbsp; ideas and debates, where diverse perspectives lead to deeper understanding and better quality results. PhonePe is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to treating all its employees and job applicants equally; regardless of&nbsp; gender, sexual preference, religion, race, color or disability. If you have a disability or special need that requires assistance or reasonable accommodation, during the application and hiring process, including support for the interview or onboarding process, </em></strong><a