-time pipelines, and developer tooling entirely on-premise. You'll build the core data infrastructure, tools, and internal products that enable hundreds of engineers, analysts, data scientists, and business teams to move faster.</p>\n<h3>What You'll Do:&nbsp;</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> Own product strategy</strong>, specs, and roadmaps for data platform components, APIs, and developer tools</li>\n<li><strong> Synthesize requirements</strong> from business/product teams and translate them into system APIs, developer interfaces, and platform capabilities</li>\n<li><strong> Work with architects</strong> and engineering leads to balance reliability, performance, technical debt, and new features</li>\n<li><strong> Design solutions</strong> for data quality, governance, cataloging, and pipeline efficiency at petabyte scale</li>\n<li><strong> Define and track platform health metrics</strong>: latency, query performance, uptime, adoption, resource efficiency</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Must Haves:</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Product Management Experience</li>\n<ol>\n<li>1-3 year as PM/APM with product ownership, OR&nbsp;</li>\n<li>2-3 years as Data/Backend Engineer with PM work (PRDs, roadmaps, user research)</li>\n</ol>\n<li>Technical Stack Depth</li>\n<ol>\n<li>Deep understanding: ETL/ELT pipelines, data warehousing, data lakes/lakehouses</li>\n<li>Advanced SQL (query optimization, not just SELECT statements)&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Hands-on with ONE of: Hive/Spark/Hadoop/HDFS, Snowflake/Databricks/BigQuery, or Airflow/DBT/Kafka/Trino&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Understands how data systems work end-to-end (not just BI layer)</li>\n</ol>\n<li>Problem-First Thinking</li>\n<ol>\n<li>Asks clarifying questions before solutions (WHO, WHAT, WHEN, WHY, HOW)&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Articulates problems \u2192 solutions \u2192 outcomes (not feature lists)&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Synthesizes requirements from diverse stakeholders into clear product specs</li>\n</ol>\n<li>Structured Approach</li>\n<ol>\n<li>Breaks down ambiguous problems systematically</li>\n<li>States assumptions explicitly and validates them</li>\n<li>Thinks in MVP phases and iterations</li>\n</ol>\n<li>Technical Communication</li>\n<ol>\n<li>Holds technical discussions with engineers/architects</li>\n<li>Translates business needs into system specs, APIs, and developer interfaces</li>\n<li>Writes clear PRDs, specs, and documentation</li>\n</ol>\n</ol>\n<h3>Good To Haves:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>TB/PB-scale data systems experience</li>\n<li>On-prem stack: Hive, Spark, HDFS, Hadoop, Impala (cloud experience acceptable if fundamentals strong)</li>\n<li>Built internal developer tools, APIs, or self-service platforms</li>\n<li>Data governance: cataloging, lineage, access controls, metadata management, observability</li>\n<li>AI-native workflow: Active user of ChatGPT/Claude/GitHub Copilot; bonus for GenAI features (RAG, LLM apps)</li>\n<li>High-potential signals: Published work, side projects, led cross-functional teams</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Why Join?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Unmatched scale: Petabyte-scale data infrastructure, real-time pipelines at national scale</li>\n<li>Open-source stack: Massive on-premise deployments (Hive, Spark, HDFS, Hadoop)</li>\n<li>High impact: Enable every engineering, analytics, and business team to move faster</li>\n<li>Ownership + mentorship: Core platform modules with structured career growth</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><strong>PhonePe Full Time Employee Benefits (Not applicable for Intern or Contract Roles)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Insurance Benefits - </strong>Medical Insurance, Critical Illness Insurance, Accidental Insurance, Life Insurance</li>\n<li><strong>Wellness Program -</strong> Employee Assistance Program, Onsite Medical Center, Emergency Support System</li>\n<li><strong>Parental Support - </strong>Maternity Benefit, Paternity Benefit Program, Adoption Assistance Program, Day-care Support Program</li>\n<li><strong>Mobility Benefits - </strong>Relocation benefits, Transfer Support Policy, 