      "description": "<p><strong>About Druva<br></strong>Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva\u2019s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.<br>Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.</p>\n<p>Visit<a href=\"https://www.druva.com/\">&nbsp;druva.com</a>&nbsp;and follow us on&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/\">LinkedIn</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://twitter.com/druvainc\">X</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/\">Facebook</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>About the Team</strong></p>\n<p>You will be part of a high-impact, fast moving product management team driving our portfolio of products serving partner needs around Data Protection, Cyber Recovery and Response,&nbsp;Disaster Recovery and Governance .</p>\n<p><strong>Role Purpose &amp; Impact</strong></p>\n<p>We are looking for a Product Manager to help build and scale Druva's Managed Service Provider (MSP) platform. You will work closely with MSP partners, internal stakeholders,&nbsp;engineering, UX, sales, and customer success to understand partner needs and translate them into product capabilities that simplify service delivery, improve operational efficiency, and&nbsp;accelerate partner growth.</p>\n<p>This is an excellent opportunity for someone with 3\u20135 years of Product Management experience who enjoys working directly with customers, solving real business problems, and shipping products that have measurable business impact.</p>\n<p><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p>\n<p>\u25cf Partner with MSPs, distributors, aggregators and internal teams to understand customer workflows, operational challenges, and emerging market needs.<br>\u25cf Gather product requirements through partner interviews and engagements, competitive&nbsp;research, and data analysis.<br>\u25cf Prioritize features in collaboration with Engineering and Product leadership.<br>\u25cf Write clear Product Requirement Documents (PRDs), user stories, and acceptance&nbsp;criteria.<br>\u25cf Drive execution from concept through launch using Agile methodologies.<br>\u25cf Collaborate with UX to design intuitive multi-tenant experiences for MSP administrators.<br>\u25cf Work with Sales, Customer Success, and Support to identify product improvements and&nbsp;increase partner adoption.<br>\u25cf Define success metrics and analyze product telemetry to guide roadmap decisions.<br>\u25cf Assist with product launches by creating enablement material, release notes, and&nbsp;customer-facing documentation.<br>\u25cf Represent the voice of MSP customers during planning and sprint reviews.<br>\u25cf Stay current on trends in managed services, SaaS, cloud infrastructure, backup, cyber&nbsp;resilience, and channel ecosystems.</p>\n<p><strong>What makes you a great fit</strong></p>\n<p>\u25cf 3\u20135 years of Product Management experience building B2B SaaS products.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience working with Managed Service Providers (MSPs), Distributors, Value Added Resellers (VARs), or other channel partners preferred</li>\n<li>Experience with building products for marketplaces, integrations, or multi-tenant&nbsp;SaaS platforms preferred</li>\n</ul>\n<p>\u25cf Bachelor's degree in Engineering, Computer Science, or related field.<br>\u25cf Experience writing detailed product requirements and working closely with engineering teams.<br>\u25cf Strong understanding of Agile development methodologies.<br>\u25cf Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills.<br>\u25cf Strong communication and stakeholder management skills.<br>\u25cf Passion for understanding customer problems and turning them into simple product experiences.</p>\n<p><strong>What Success Looks Like in the Role</strong></p>\n<p>\u25cf Help solve key challenges around MSP scalability, workflow simplification, integrations, and partner experience.<br>\u25cf Become the trusted owner of a product area, delivering customer-focused solutions that&nbsp;drive measurable business outcomes.<br>\u25cf Build strong partnerships across Engineering, Design, Sales, Customer Success, and&nbsp;partners to execute effectively.<br>\u25cf Use customer feedback, market insights, and product data to prioritize initiatives that&nbsp;improve adoption, retention, and revenue.<br>\u25cf Deliver roadmap commitments with high quality, proactively managing trade-offs, risks,&nbsp;and dependencies.<br>\u25cf Demonstrable impact on product KPIs (e.g., adoption, engagement, retention, revenue,&nbsp;partner satisfaction).</p>\n<p><strong>Why You\u2019ll Love Working Here</strong></p>\n<p>Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You\u2019ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new&nbsp;ideas into products customers can rely on.&nbsp;If you\u2019re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation,&nbsp;collaboration, accountability, and growth\u2014where you\u2019ll be trusted to lead and empowered to&nbsp;build\u2014you\u2019ll thrive at Druva.</p>\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
