recise prompts, and subsequently automating those test cases using AI.</p>\n<p><strong>Operating Systems &amp; Core Concepts:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Knowledge of working with Docker, Linux, Windows</li>\n<li>Good knowledge of networking and cloud architecture fundamentals, preferably with exposure to AWS and/or Azure services (networking, storage, compute).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Programming &amp; Automation:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Proficiency in Python or Java (Python preferred).</li>\n<li>Strong Shell scripting ability.</li>\n<li>Hands-on experience with SQL databases.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Testing skills &amp; Tools:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Strong experience in REST API testing and backend automation.</li>\n<li>Experience in UI automation (Selenium / Playwright preferred)</li>\n<li>Proficiency with tools like Git, Jira, XRay, Jenkins etc.</li>\n<li>Strong analytical and debugging skills.</li>\n<li>Exposure to Load and Performance testing and related tools</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Desirable Skills&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Understanding of CI/CD Pipelines.</li>\n<li>Experience testing workloads on AWS/Azure, including basic resource setup, debugging and monitoring (Cloudwatch etc).</li>\n<li>Exposure to generative AI using Cursor or similar tools.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Qualification:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>B.Tech / B.E / M.E./ M.Tech or equivalent.</li>\n</ul>",
