      "description": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The <strong>Customer Retention Manager</strong> is responsible for reducing churn, improving customer health, and protecting recurring revenue through early risk detection, cross\u2011functional mitigation, and scalable retention programs. The role partners closely with Renewals, Customer Success, Customer Engagement, Competitive Intelligence, and Pricing &amp; Packaging to orchestrate coordinated customer\u2011save strategies.</p>\n<p>This role also provides <strong>renewal objection handling expertise</strong>, enabling teams to navigate downsells, downgrades, competitive threats, pricing pushback, TCO/ROI concerns, and budget constraints. The ideal candidate excels at influencing cross\u2011functional teams, handling commercial risk, and translating customer insights into save actions.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h1><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h1>\n<h2><strong>1. Churn Risk Identification &amp; Health Intelligence</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Maintain a standardized <strong>customer risk scoring framework</strong> leveraging health signals, product usage, support patterns, sentiment, and competitive exposure.</li>\n<li>Identify early risk indicators (e.g., discount cliffs, adoption gaps, under-deployed licenses, sponsor turnover).</li>\n<li>Partner with Renewal Ops, Data team to automate risk workflows in Salesforce</li>\n<li>Collaborate with Competitive Intelligence to map <strong>competitive displacement trends</strong> and update counter strategies.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br><br><br></p>\n<h2><strong>2. Cross\u2011Functional Risk Orchestration (Renewals, CS, CI, Pricing)</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Lead <strong>weekly renewal risk reviews/war rooms</strong> with Renewals, CSMs/CEMs, and Sales to align on mitigation actions.</li>\n<li>Build <strong>account-level mitigation plans</strong> that include adoption interventions, executive alignment, value reinforcement, and commercial flexibility.</li>\n<li>Partner with Pricing &amp; Packaging and Deal Desk to design <strong>controlled commercial offers</strong> (e.g., term/ramp, New Product Introductions, New SKU Impact, Product Bundling etc).</li>\n<li>Escalate systemic product, billing, or support issues and track resolution.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h2><strong>3. Renewal Objection Handling&nbsp;</strong></h2>\n<p>Serve as the subject\u2011matter expert for Renewals by providing guidance, playbooks, and strategic support to overcome critical renewal objections.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Diagnose downsell and downgrade risks</strong>, recommend right\u2011sizing strategies, and deliver value\u2011based narratives to reinforce ROI and prevent unnecessary revenue loss.</li>\n<li><strong>Partner with Competitive Intelligence</strong> to address competitive pricing challenges, coach teams on TCO and switching\u2011cost comparisons, and collaborate with Pricing on controlled incentive structures.</li>\n<li><strong>Provide Renewals reps with ROI models, justification materials, payment\u2011flexibility options, pricing guardrails, and negotiation strategies</strong> to resolve budget and pricing objections while protecting retention revenue.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h2><strong>4. Preemptive Retention Programs</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Launch and manage <strong>proactive churn-prevention programs</strong>, such as:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Early renewal health checks</li>\n<li>Competitive threat campaigns</li>\n<li>Discount cliff mitigation</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Develop and maintain <strong>risk playbooks</strong> for teams to execute consistently.</li>\n<li>Partner with Enablement to deliver training on objection handling and retention strategies.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h2><strong>5. Insights, Reporting &amp; Executive Readouts</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliver monthly churn insights including root causes, save rates, objection trends, and program impact.</li>\n<li>Own cohort analyses, risk heatmaps, and retention dashboards.</li>\n<li>Provide actionable 