      "description": "<p><strong>Intern \u2013 CA Industrial Trainee (Accounting / Reporting)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>About the Role</strong></p>\n<p>We are offering an excellent learning opportunity within our International Accounting &amp; Reporting team based at Bangalore. Designed specifically for CA students seeking industrial training, this role supports our U.S. GAAP accounting team or International Reporting team. You will step into a global corporate environment, partner with team members worldwide, and gain hands-on exposure to corporate accounting principles, change management, and complex issue resolution. We are looking for motivated individuals who thrive in a fast-paced setting and embrace new challenges.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>About the Team</strong></p>\n<p>Our global accounting team is the backbone of our financial reporting. We are responsible for finalizing the financial statements for all subsidiaries across North America, EMEA, and APAC, ensuring strict adherence to the required GAAP in each country. This team drives compliance with regulatory guidelines and corporate accounting policies. From managing accurate and timely book closures to overseeing financial audits, GL management, and reconciliations, we maintain and elevate the overall control environment.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>What You\u2019ll Be Doing</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Support the Close Process:</strong> Assist the team with month-end and quarter-end U.S. GAAP close processes and related departmental responsibilities.</li>\n<li><strong>Execute Accounting Tasks:</strong> Participate in the accurate and timely execution of close procedures to ensure highly reliable financial reporting.</li>\n<li><strong>Collaborate Globally:</strong> Work closely with the broader corporate accounting team, shadowing experts to support a seamless monthly book closure.</li>\n<li><strong>Learn Risk Assessment:</strong> Help analyze accounts to assess financial risks and learn to a