ment development plans to enhance individual and team capabilities in an inclusive environment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Customer Engagement and Relationship Management:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Build and maintain strong relationships with key decision-makers in target accounts, demonstrating a deep understanding of their unique business needs, challenges, and pain points.</li>\n<li>Collaborate closely with the marketing and pre-sales teams to develop persuasive value propositions, presentations, and sales collateral that embrace diversity and cater to the Mid-Market segment.</li>\n<li>Ensure outstanding levels of customer satisfaction by delivering exceptional service, promptly resolving issues, and acting as a champion for customers within the organization, fostering an inclusive and customer-centric approach.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Sales Operations and Forecasting:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Monitor sales activity, pipeline, and revenue forecasts meticulously to ensure accurate and timely reporting, embracing a data-driven and diverse perspective.</li>\n<li>Leverage CRM systems and sales analytics tools effectively to track sales performance, identify trends, and optimize sales processes with an inclusive lens.</li>\n<li>Collaborate seamlessly with cross-functional teams, including finance, legal, and operations, to ensure seamless sales operations and equitable deal closure.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Qualifications and Skills:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Demonstrable track record of success in sales leadership roles within the enterprise SaaS space, ideally selling into IT / Security.</li>\n<li>5+ years minimum sales leadership experience. We do also welcome strong first-line sales leaders with a proven record of building and coaching high-performing teams who are ready to step up into their first 2nd-line leadership role, as well as candidates with 2+ years of existing 2nd-line experience.</li>\n<li>Recent, direct quota-carrying experience as an individual contributor at