n all creative materials to ensure they meet Elastic\u2019s standards for quality, accuracy, and brand consistency.</li>\n<li>Build efficient creative processes that help the team move faster without sacrificing quality.</li>\n<li>Partner closely with marketing, product, executives, and agencies to deliver strategic creative.</li>\n<li>Champion experimentation, AI-powered workflows, and modern creative practices.</li>\n<li>Manage relationships with external creative agencies and media partners to ensure high-quality execution of deliverables</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>What You'll Bring</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience leading in-house creative teams, ideally in B2B technology.</li>\n<li>Exceptional portfolio demonstrating strong brand thinking and execution.</li>\n<li>Deep understanding of technical audiences and enterprise marketing.</li>\n<li>Ability to balance creative innovation with operational discipline.</li>\n<li>Strong coaching, communication, and stakeholder management skills.</li>\n<li>Curiosity, adaptability, and a desire to continuously evolve how creative work gets done.<br><br></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>#LI-JM5</p><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br>Compensation for this role is in the form of base salary.&nbsp; This role does not have a variable compensation component.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The typical starting salary range for new hires in this role is listed below.&nbsp; In select locations (including Seattle WA, Los Angeles CA, the San Francisco Bay Area CA, and the New York City Metro Area), an alternate range may apply as specified below.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These ranges represent </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">the lowest to highest salary we reasonably and in good faith believe we would pay for this role at the time of this posting.&nbsp; We may ultimately 